:1445202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444747-the-sabbat-paths-and-what-we-know?p=1444771#post1444771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hopefully there will be options for non-human touchstones. I hate mooning over Bella Swans. Bella Swans should be something the Sabbat mock the Cammies for.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I Hope there's actual repercussions for not being on humanity so Sabbat don't seem like the obvious superior choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T20:35:28-07:00","id":1445206,"title":"","content":"That's why I love Long Road Out of Hell. Beast Marks are waaaaayyyyyy more fun to roleplay than mooning over Bella Swans.<br /> <br /> Right now I'm playing a character with Convictions of Steel, Animal Instinct, and The Need to Feed, and it is sooooooo much fun roleplaying all three Beast Marks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 04-21-2021, 11:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T20:45:07-07:00","id":1445210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444747-the-sabbat-paths-and-what-we-know?p=1445202#post1445202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I Hope there's actual repercussions for not being on humanity so Sabbat don't seem like the obvious superior choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, Paths should be a roleplaying choice.<br /> <br /> They're only &quot;easier&quot; than Humanity if you're a homicidal psychopath.<br /> <br /> You may not get punished for taking a human life but if you ever give money to charity, you'll go wassail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T21:04:00-07:00","id":1445211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444747-the-sabbat-paths-and-what-we-know?p=1445210#post1445210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind you, Paths should be a roleplaying choice.<br /> <br /> They're only &quot;easier&quot; than Humanity if you're a homicidal psychopath.<br /> <br /> You may not get punished for taking a human life but if you ever give money to charity, you'll go wassail.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's only true for a couple of paths. For most, indiscriminate killing is still a sin for one reason or other. Keep in mind, any viable path must provide a crutch to resist the two great urges of vampires: the urge to destroy anything that makes you even a little angry, and the urge to utterly glut yourself when even slightly hungry. Any path that doesn't do this fails to prevent wighthood, because you have nothing to cling to when those urges happen.<br /> <br /> Humanity-&quot;I will not destroy anything that makes me even slightly angry, or utterly glut myself when even slightly hungry, because that is evil. I will remain a decent human being, not a monster.&quot;<br /> <br /> Honorable Accord-&quot;I will not destroy anything that makes me even slightly angry, or utterly glut myself when even slightly hungry, because that would cause me to break my sacred oaths, either directly, or by bringing hunters down on the Sect and Pack I have sworn to protect. I will be a noble knight, courageous, controlled, and true to my word.&quot;<br /> <br /> Feral Heart=&quot;I will not destroy anything that makes me even slightly angry, or utterly glut myself when even slightly hungry, because that is suicidal, and cunning, far-seeing, alert predators are not suicidal.I will be a wolf, loyal to pack, mate, and cubs, not a mindless maniac&quot;<br /> <br /> Even Cathari demands you try to corrupt humans, which is rather difficult if you kill them in the most innocent stage of their lives.<br /> <br /> Most paths don't care one way or the other if you give to charity, though it's hard to imagine a dedicated path follower caring about humans enough to do so.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T21:27:58-07:00","id":1445216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444747-the-sabbat-paths-and-what-we-know?p=1445211#post1445211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's only true for a couple of paths. For most, indiscriminate killing is still a sin for one reason or other. Keep in mind, any viable path must provide a crutch to resist the two great urges of vampires: the urge to destroy anything that makes you even a little angry, and the urge to utterly glut yourself when even slightly hungry. Any path that doesn't do this fails to prevent wighthood, because you have nothing to cling to when those urges happen.<br /> <br /> Humanity-&quot;I will not destroy anything that makes me even slightly angry, or utterly glut myself when even slightly hungry, because that is evil. I will remain a decent human being, not a monster.&quot;<br /> <br /> Honorable Accord-&quot;I will not destroy anything that makes me even slightly angry, or utterly glut myself when even slightly hungry, because that would cause me to break my sacred oaths, either directly, or by bringing hunters down on the Sect and Pack I have sworn to protect. I will be a noble knight, courageous, controlled, and true to my word.&quot;<br /> <br /> Feral Heart=&quot;I will not destroy anything that makes me even slightly angry, or utterly glut myself when even slightly hungry, because that is suicidal, and cunning, far-seeing, alert predators are not suicidal.I will be a wolf, loyal to pack, mate, and cubs, not a mindless maniac&quot;<br /> <br /> Even Cathari demands you try to corrupt humans, which is rather difficult if you kill them in the most innocent stage of their lives.<br /> <br /> Most paths don't care one way or the other if you give to charity, though it's hard to imagine a dedicated path follower caring about humans enough to do so.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well I'm not speaking literally but the idea is that following a Path should be every bit as difficult as following Humanity, if not more so, it's just the tenets are going to be easier in some respects (violence, feeding, and so on) and much more difficult in others.<br /> <br /> Paths shouldn't be Easy Mode, they're just a different mode for people who want to play monstrous or alien Kindred and not wassail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T21:38:19-07:00","id":1445217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444747-the-sabbat-paths-and-what-we-know?p=1445210#post1445210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind you, Paths should be a roleplaying choice.<br /> <br /> They're only &quot;easier&quot; than Humanity if you're a homicidal psychopath.<br /> <br /> You may not get punished for taking a human life but if you ever give money to charity, you'll go wassail.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And the person who would follow that path is never giving to charity so...or give you a 1 hour rant on how htey are doing it for themselves with heavy citations from Ayn Rand.<br /> <br /> My issue has been much of the Flaws of being on paths are externalized and require more ST engagement rather than random rolls and breaking wrong. For example being on a path is.. much more likely to get you noticed by hunters that doesn't really work as a balancing feature in table top unless you are willing to have players just get ganked in their sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T21:48:48-07:00","id":1445218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444747-the-sabbat-paths-and-what-we-know?p=1445217#post1445217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And the person who would follow that path is never giving to charity so...or give you a 1 hour rant on how htey are doing it for themselves with heavy citations from Ayn Rand.<br /> <br /> My issue has been much of the Flaws of being on paths are externalized and require more ST engagement rather than random rolls and breaking wrong. For example being on a path is.. much more likely to get you noticed by hunters that doesn't really work as a balancing feature in table top unless you are willing to have players just get ganked in their sleep.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does require players who are committed to their characters, and willing to roleplay the weaknesses inherent in those characters. I've periodically had to remind my ST that I have to ride the wave or get a stain, and that I am at risk of frenzy at hunger 3, not 4. So even on just a mechanical level, it requires an extra level of either dedication on the players part, or memory on the ST's part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T23:32:30-07:00","id":1445229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1444747-the-sabbat-paths-and-what-we-know?p=1445218#post1445218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does require players who are committed to their characters, and willing to roleplay the weaknesses inherent in those characters. I've periodically had to remind my ST that I have to ride the wave or get a stain, and that I am at risk of frenzy at hunger 3, not 4. So even on just a mechanical level, it requires an extra level of either dedication on the players part, or memory on the ST's part.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That has been a problem in the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom